<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea steps in to support won - dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea steps in to support won - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea intervened in the interbank market in early morning trading on Monday to support the falling won against the dollar, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The central bank intervened at 845.30, traders said.</p>
<p>The won opened at a six year low of 845.50 and sank further before the central bank stepped in.</p>
<p>The previous six-year low for the won was 845.00 on December 12, traders said.</p>
<p>They said the market has been short on dollars due to large import settlements and poor sentiment towards the domestic currency.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
